cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use scruple in published research, please cite it."
title: "scruple: calibrated deductive coding with abstention and a class-conditional reliability guarantee"
abstract: >-
  scruple codes a text corpus against a researcher-written codebook, abstains on
  items whose calibrated probability falls in an uncertain band, and reports
  inter-rater reliability of the delivered dataset against a blind human gold
  sample with a class-conditional (Mondrian) error guarantee.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "PLACEHOLDER"
    given-names: "PLACEHOLDER"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/scruple-tool/scruple"
keywords:
  - qualitative research
  - content analysis
  - inter-rater reliability
  - calibration
  - selective prediction
